{#
  THE INVITATION — a BODY, not a document.

  ── WHY THIS FILE SHRANK BY TWO HUNDRED LINES ───────────────────────────────

  It used to be a complete HTML document: its own doctype, head, masthead, hero,
  footer and unsubscribe. And it was handed to `OtpService::sendBranded()`, which
  passes what it is given to `brandWrap()` — the house shell — and drops it inside
  a table cell.

  So the message that actually reached an inbox was two documents nested: the house
  pre-header strip and ink masthead, then a whole second `<html>` with a second
  masthead and a second footer, then the house footer again. Two of everything.
  The admin preview never showed it because `preview()` rendered THIS file alone,
  so the operator read one email and the recipient received another.

  Every other transactional message on this platform is a fragment — see
  `OtpService::sendPartnerConfirmation()` and the nomination confirmations. The
  campaign path is the exception and it says so: it renders a full document and
  sends through `sendRawHtml()`, which does not wrap.

  This is a fragment now, in the house idiom, and the shell is the shell.

  ── WHAT THE SHELL ALREADY PROVIDES, SO NOTHING HERE REPEATS IT ─────────────

  The wordmark, the category chip ("Invitation"), the hero image, the footer, the
  unsubscribe link, the hidden preheader, and the 600px card on its paper ground.
  This file starts at the salutation and ends at the sign-off.

  Type comes from the shell's body cell: DM Sans, 15px, 1.65, #4a5256 on white.
  Anything set here that the shell already sets is a second opinion about the same
  thing, and the two drift.
#}

<p style="margin:0 0 6px;font-family:'Playfair Display',Georgia,serif;font-size:21px;line-height:1.3;color:#10292C">{{ salutation }} {{ name }},</p>

{# The operator's sentence — the one piece of copy that changes per programme, and
   the reason the room is being filled. Set at body size and left alone. #}
<p style="margin:0 0 14px;font-size:15px;line-height:1.65;color:#4a5256">{{ witness }}</p>
<p style="margin:0 0 22px;font-size:15px;line-height:1.65;color:#4a5256">
  We would like the people who know that work best to be in the room to see it recognised.
</p>

{# ── THE EVENING ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   The house callout, which on this platform is a tinted panel with a rule down its
   leading edge — the shape used for the nomination confirmation and the partner
   reply. It carries the date, because the date is what an invitation is FOR and a
   sentence is where it goes to be missed. #}
<table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%"
       style="margin:0 0 22px;background:#f4f7f4;border-left:4px solid #237b22;border-radius:0 8px 8px 0">
  <tr>
    <td style="padding:16px 20px">
      <p style="margin:0 0 4px;font-size:10.5px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#5c7a5e">You are invited to</p>
      <p style="margin:0 0 10px;font-family:'Playfair Display',Georgia,serif;font-size:19px;line-height:1.25;color:#10292C">{{ event_title }}</p>
      <p style="margin:0;font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.6;color:#3f5a41">
        <strong style="color:#1e3b23">{{ when_day }} {{ when_date }}</strong><br>
        {{ when_time }}{% if where %} · {{ where }}{% endif %}
      </p>
    </td>
  </tr>
</table>

{# ── THE PASS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   The house button: the green pill used by the nomination and claim emails. VML
   behind it, because Outlook desktop draws a padded anchor with the background
   dropped — a bare text link where the only action is. #}
<table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" style="margin:0 0 10px">
  <tr><td>
    <!--[if mso]>
    <v:roundrect xmlns:v="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:vml" xmlns:w="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word" href="{{ id_url }}" style="height:46px;v-text-anchor:middle;width:236px" arcsize="50%" strokecolor="#237b22" fillcolor="#237b22">
      <w:anchorlock/>
      <center style="color:#ffffff;font-family:'DM Sans',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;font-weight:600">Open your pass</center>
    </v:roundrect>
    <![endif]-->
    <!--[if !mso]><!-->
    <a href="{{ id_url }}" style="display:inline-block;background:#237b22;color:#ffffff;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;font-size:15px;padding:13px 26px;border-radius:999px">Open your pass</a>
    <!--<![endif]-->
  </td></tr>
</table>
<p style="margin:0 0 24px;font-size:13.5px;line-height:1.6;color:#6b7280">
  Your seat is arranged — there is no ticket for you to buy. The pass is a live page:
  open it on your phone at the door.
</p>

{# ── THE ASK ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   Their reference is one string doing two jobs: their identity at the door and the
   code their guests spend. Gold-ruled rather than green, because it is the one
   thing on the page that is not about them. #}
<table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%"
       style="margin:0 0 14px;background:#fdf8ec;border-left:4px solid #f3b416;border-radius:0 8px 8px 0">
  <tr>
    <td style="padding:16px 20px">
      <p style="margin:0 0 6px;font-size:10.5px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#8a6205">Bring your people</p>
      <p style="margin:0 0 4px;font-family:Consolas,'Courier New',monospace;font-size:19px;letter-spacing:2px;color:#10292C">{{ reference }}</p>
      <p style="margin:0;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;color:#7a6636">{{ discount }}% off · up to {{ quota }} guests</p>
    </td>
  </tr>
</table>
<p style="margin:0 0 10px;font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.65;color:#4a5256">
  Share it with the people you want in the room. It takes {{ discount }}% off their tickets,
  for up to {{ quota }} of them{% if tier_line %}{{ tier_line }}{% endif %}.
</p>
{# The secondary action gets its own line. Left inline it landed mid-sentence and then
   wrapped, so an underlined green link broke across two lines in the middle of a
   paragraph — which reads as damage rather than as the second thing to do. #}
<p style="margin:0 0 26px;font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.65">
  <a href="{{ events_url }}" style="color:#237b22;font-weight:600;text-decoration:underline">Send them to the tickets&nbsp;→</a>
</p>

<p style="margin:0 0 4px;font-size:15px;line-height:1.65;color:#4a5256">
  We would be honoured to have you with us. The formal invitation is attached, for your records.
</p>
<p style="margin:0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.65;color:#10292C">
  With respect,<br><strong style="font-weight:600">Africa GATES</strong>
</p>
